# 550-NET-0058 — A read-only Wi-Fi client, and its refusal of changes checked — done

**Type:** network (`wlan`), with `init`'s grant and the shell's lending · **Owner:** `NET` · **Priority:** P3 · **Status:** done (2026-11-05) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [550](../issues/550-network-on-real-hardware.md) · **Constitution:** MC-6.1, MC-12.2

**Split from:** [550-NET-0035](550-NET-0035-the-stations-country.done), whose criterion "a read-only client is refused" could not be tested.

## Problem

- **`wlan` keeps two rights apart.** A client badged `BADGE_WIFI` reads: it scans, and reads the status, the countries and the country. One badged `BADGE_WIFI_CHANGE` may also join, leave, forget and set the country (`may_change` in `wlan/src/main.rs`).
- **No program holds a reading client:**
  - `init` lends `wlan` only with `BADGE_WIFI_CHANGE`, to the shell and to `link`;
  - the shell lends that same client to a program that asks for Wi-Fi (`REQUEST_WIFI`). Its slot has no right to badge, so it cannot make a narrower copy.
- **So the refusal is untested,** and a program that only shows the network gets the right to change it (MC-6.1).

## Plan

1. **A reading client for programs** that only look, such as a status line. The shell cannot narrow its own copy: a badge is set once and a copy keeps it (`kernel/src/scheduler.rs`, MC-3.4). An unbadged client with the badge right would widen the shell instead: without `BADGE_WIFI`, `wlan` takes a client for the network stack's card (`net.wit`). So the station mints the reading client itself:
   - **`wifi.wit` 1.3 `reader`** (`NET`): `wlan` mints one `BADGE_WIFI` client from its own endpoint at its start and answers it to any client of the interface; `unsupported` when its endpoint has no right to badge.
   - **`init`'s grant** (`KRN`): `wlan`'s endpoint with `ALL | CAP_BADGE`, as `blockstore`'s (308-KRN-0184), and a request bit for a program that asks for the reading client alone. Made as [550-KRN-0213](550-KRN-0213-the-stations-endpoint-may-badge-its-reading-client.done).
   - **The shell's lending** (`APP`): for that bit, it asks `reader` and lends what it gets. Numbered as [550-APP-0124](550-APP-0124-the-shell-lends-a-reading-wifi-client.done).
2. **`wlan`'s answers to it:** every changing call (`join`, `leave`, `forget`, `set-country`) is `denied`, and nothing changes.
3. **A QEMU check** in the `net` suite, with a program that holds the reading client: `netcheck wifi`, lent the changing client (`REQUEST_WIFI`), asks `reader`, drops what it was lent and works through what it got.

## Acceptance criteria

- **QEMU, x86 and aarch64:** a program with the reading client reads the status and the country; `set-country` and `join` from it are `denied`, and the station's country and link are as before.
- **Docs:** `docs/network` and `docs/profile/bootstrap.md` name the client and who holds it.

## Progress

- **2026-11-05, on `claude/relaxed-meitner-5bmhpz` at eca06c5c3:**
  - `idl/wifi.wit` 1.3 `reader` and its generated `libmind/src/idl/wifi.rs`;
  - `wlan` minting the reading client;
  - `netcheck wifi`, and `wificheck wifi` in the `net` suite's joined-station check;
  - `docs/network/station.md` 0.2, and the `wifi` rows of `docs/idl/README.md` and `docs/profile/bootstrap.md`.
- **Tested in this session's container (4 CPUs),** with the branch on `main` at 27cebd982 and `init`'s line from the KRN request applied but not committed:
  - the `net` suite passed on x86 (35 checks) and on aarch64 (32), with `wificheck wifi` among them;
  - the host tests passed.
- **Not done yet:**
  - `init`'s grant (`KRN`). Without it `reader` answers `unsupported` and the new check fails, so the landing request waits for it.
  - The request bit (`KRN`) and the shell's lending (`APP`): a program that does not first hold the changing client cannot get a reading one yet.

## Resolution

Landed in `main` 7f260e43 (landing round 7f260e43), from `claude/relaxed-meitner-5bmhpz` fe4732ee, with [550-KRN-0213](550-KRN-0213-the-stations-endpoint-may-badge-its-reading-client.done) in the same round.

- **`idl/wifi.wit` 1.3 `reader`** (minor), with its generated `libmind/src/idl/wifi.rs`: a client of the station that only reads, `BADGE_WIFI`, or `unsupported`.
- **`wlan`** (`wlan/src/main.rs`):
  - it mints that client once at its start, from its own endpoint, which `init` grants with the badge right (550-KRN-0213);
  - it never mints `BADGE_WIFI_CHANGE` or an unbadged client;
  - it answers that client to any client of the interface;
  - without the right it logs `[WLAN] NO READING CLIENT`, and `reader` answers `unsupported`.
- **`netcheck wifi`:** takes the reading client through the changing one it was lent and drops that one; reads the link and the country through it; is denied `join`, `leave`, `forget` and `set-country`; and finds the station as it was.
- **The `net` suite** (`tests/qemu_smoke.py`): `wificheck wifi` in the joined-station check over `wlansim`.
- **Docs:**
  - `docs/network/station.md` 0.2, its section "Who may change the station";
  - the `wifi` row of `docs/idl/README.md`;
  - the `wlan` row of `docs/profile/bootstrap.md`: who may change the station, and the one badge `wlan` mints.
- **Tested** in this session's container (4 CPUs, QEMU 8.2.2 under TCG) on fe4732ee:
  - the `net` suite passed on x86 (35 checks) and aarch64 (32);
  - the host tests' Rust tests passed. One Python test of EFF's, `effector_server_test.py`, fails under this container's Python 3.13 and OpenSSL 3.5 on `main` as well, and was reported to EFF.

  The round's gate ran the candidate on the maintainer's machines. These are test results on those configurations, not a proof (MC-12.2).
- **Left, not this task's:** the shell's lending of the reading client for `REQUEST_WIFI_READ` is [550-APP-0124](550-APP-0124-the-shell-lends-a-reading-wifi-client.done). Until it lands, a program gets the reading client only through the changing client it was lent.

